# Ground Beef and Bean Burritos

Based on a recipe by Ali Slagle, inspired by Los Angeles-style burritos. Yields 6 burritos.

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 pound [ground beef]{ ing="ground-beef" }
- [ ] 1 medium [yellow or white onion]{ ing="onion" }, finely chopped
- [ ] 1 1/2 teaspoons [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1/2 teaspoon [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, or chipotle or ancho chile powder
- [ ] 1/2 teaspoon [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] [Kosher salt]{ ing="salt" } and [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 (15-ounce) can [black or pinto beans]{ ing="black-or-pinto-beans" }
- [ ] 1 large [tomato]{ ing="tomato" }, coarsely chopped
- [ ] 2 teaspoons [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" } or apple cider vinegar
- [ ] 6 burrito-size (about 10-inch) [flour tortillas]{ ing="flour-tortillas" }
- [ ] 2 cups (8 ounces) shredded [Monterey Jack]{ ing="monterey-jack" } or Mexican blend cheese
- [ ] [Hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" }, for drizzling (optional)

## Recipe

1. In a large skillet, press the [beef]{ ing="ground-beef" } into an even layer to fill the skillet. Sprinkle with the [onion]{ ing="onion" }. Cook over medium-high heat, undisturbed, until the meat is deeply browned underneath, 6 to 8 minutes. Sprinkle with the [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" } and [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" } and season with [salt]{ ing="salt" } and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }. Break up the beef into small pieces, then cook, stirring occasionally, until the onion is softened and the spices are fragrant, 2 to 4 minutes
1. Add the [beans]{ ing="black-or-pinto-beans" }, including the liquid, and the [tomato]{ ing="tomato" } and simmer, stirring and scraping up browned bits, until the liquid has evaporated and the mixture starts to sizzle, 8 to 10 minutes. Turn off the heat, stir in the [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" } and season with salt and pepper
1. Arrange the [tortillas]{ ing="flour-tortillas" } on a clean work surface. Sprinkle half the [cheese]{ ing="monterey-jack" } across the center of the tortillas, left to right, leaving a 1-inch border. Top each with 2/3 cup of the beef-bean mixture, followed by the remaining cheese. Drizzle on [hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" } (if using). Fold the tortilla's short sides over the filling, then fold the bottom of the tortilla snugly over the filling. Tightly roll away from you until the burrito is sealed. Repeat with the other tortillas
1. When ready to eat, in a nonstick skillet over medium, place the burritos seam side down. Cook, turning occasionally, until golden all over, 3 to 5 minutes. Serve with desired toppings

## Notes

- Make ahead: prepare through step 3. Let cool slightly, then wrap in aluminum foil. Refrigerate for up to 24 hours or freeze for up to 3 months. To reheat, remove the foil and wrap the burrito in a damp paper towel. Microwave, seam side down, until warm, 1 to 4 minutes. Remove the towel and continue to step 4
- The filling eschews guacamole, sour cream, rice and raw vegetables, which means it freezes well for up to three months
- Feel free to swap the seared ground beef for a stewed meat like birria or tinga de pollo, or make it vegetarian with just beans and cheese
